# s4_plaintext_free_early (off-path)
#
# basis      s3_beaver_reveal_inplace peak 2693096 kB; single pool (host). Peak phase per replicate:
#   run1  polled max 2673200 at t=22.71s  between after_input_encrypt and after_inference
#   run2  polled max 2684528 at t=15.25s  between after_model_load  and after_model_convert
#   run3  polled max 2678004 at t=15.56s  between after_model_load  and after_model_convert
#            humps level within 0.7%; embedding hump flat (probe_embed_forward_cpu: VmHWM 2684832 at entry).
# object     conversion hump: live torch tensors 481 MB at RSS 1992 MB (~1.5 GB ONNX serialisation and
#            protobuf). Nameable: plaintext model 433250304 B, released by s1 after from_onnx parses.
# fix        release before the parse; pytorch_model.training captured first (Dropout). Free.
# expected   peak unchanged (inference hump level); measures the two-hump floor.
#
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: libc10.so+0x4a675
OMP_NUM_THREADS=8
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_early_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,beaver_reveal_inplace_cpu
